      "side": 1,
      "message": "The name `rust_target_mut()` sounds like a regular mutable getter for an already-initialized target, whereas it actually claims uninitialized storage once and eagerly sets `rust_target_initialized_ \u003d true` before the caller runs `std::ptr::write`. Calling it twice hits `DCHECK`, and any early return before `ptr::write` would cause `~Item()` to drop uninitialized memory.\n\nCould we rename it to something like `claim_rust_target_storage()` / `init_rust_target_storage()`, document the single-use initialization contract in `item.h`, and mark `rust_target_mut` as `unsafe fn` in `bridge.rs`?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4d76ec1fa4e5ed9efae3f550c70af5f9039dfdf4",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
