      "writtenOn": "2026-11-27T01:59:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why does `rust_target_storage_` live on `Item` rather than `Target`?\n\nPutting 48 bytes + `bool` (+ padding \u003d 56 bytes) on `Item` increases the size of every `Config`, `Toolchain`, and `Pool` instance as well (large builds can have tens of thousands of `Config`s), and currently `bridge.rs` and the naming (`rust_target()`, `FfiTarget`, `kRustTargetSize`) are `Target`-specific. If this is intentionally on `Item` for upcoming `Config` support (e.g. depending on configs from Starlark), could we document that in a comment/commit message? Otherwise, moving it to `Target` would save memory and keep the API tighter.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4d76ec1fa4e5ed9efae3f550c70af5f9039dfdf4",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
